## DES-M5-CI-008: Candidate gate terminal result normalizer
Responsibilities: Convert every normal or abnormal gate subprocess outcome into a validated candidate result or bounded diagnostic failure without secondary workflow exceptions.
Interfaces: `CandidateGateCommandOutcome`, `runCandidateGateCommand()` and `normalizeCandidateGateReport()` in `packages/analysis/src/candidate-gate.ts`; the built `dist/packages/analysis/src/candidate-gate.js` entry used by the `Run closed verification matrix` step; dependency-free `.github/scripts/write-candidate-gate-runner-failure.mjs`; signing, artifact upload and terminal enforcement steps in `.github/workflows/candidate-gate.yml`; `TEST-M5-CI-MATRIX-ERROR-001` in `tests/candidate-gate-workflow-errors.test.ts`.
Constraints: `runCandidateGateCommand()` owns spawn, timeout and incremental stdout/stderr processing and returns `{ stdoutPath, stderrPath, stdoutTail, stderrTail, stdoutSha256, stderrSha256, tailsDropped, resultTextDropped, exitCode, signal, timedOut }`. Raw streams are spooled to runner-temporary regular files with exclusive creation, no symlink following and a 100,000,000-byte cap per stream while SHA-256 is updated incrementally; they are not retained completely in memory. Crossing a cap terminates the subprocess and enters the non-zero-exit abnormal case. The normalizer parses only the complete raw stdout spool and never parses a redacted tail. It removes both spool files after result persistence. Redaction covers the closed enumerated representations: exact configured secret values, their JSON string encodings, ANSI-stripped forms, GitHub token lexical forms, and authorization-header values within each stream; it does not claim to reconstruct a secret split between stdout and stderr or an undeclared encoding. The streaming redactor uses an 8,192-character maximum carry/lookbehind, redacts before a fixed 20,000-character ring tail, and records whether non-tail content was discarded. Every free-text string copied from parsed output into `candidate-gate-result.json`, including check summaries, diagnostics, original domain messages and CLI error messages, passes through the same closed redaction before persistence; identifiers, status enums, numbers and digests are copied only after type validation. If any configured representation exceeds the carry, normalization cannot safely complete, or an authorization/token candidate exceeds the lookbehind, both diagnostic tails and all parsed free-text fields are omitted, `tailsDropped: true` and `resultTextDropped: true` are recorded, and complete raw digests plus fail status remain. Tests cover a valid normal report larger than 20,000 characters, a valid report containing a configured secret whose raw JSON remains parseable while both its diagnostic tail and persisted parsed fields are secret-free, raw/JSON-escaped/multiline/ANSI-interleaved configured representations crossing chunk and eventual-tail boundaries, unknown encodings remaining outside the claim, stream-cap termination, overlong representation/lookbehind fail-closed text omission, and absence of every configured secret representation from the final result and uploaded envelope. The workflow imports the built module after the mandatory build step and passes the complete outcome metadata to the normalizer. If module import or wrapper startup fails, the dependency-free fallback writes fixed `CANDIDATE_GATE_REPORT_INVALID` / `GATE_RUNNER_UNAVAILABLE` metadata with no stdout/stderr content, then exits non-zero; its focused test deletes or corrupts the built entry and proves no stream or secret is persisted. Classification precedence is deterministic: timed out, signal, empty stdout, malformed JSON, CLI `{error}` envelope, missing `checks`, non-array `checks`, then valid normal report; a valid normal report is classified from required checks even when the subprocess exit is non-zero, preserving its redacted check diagnostics. The normalizer returns available redacted original domain code/message, exit/signal/timeout metadata and the complete raw-stream digests. The result writer always creates `candidate-gate-result.json`; signing/upload may retain a failing diagnostic envelope, but ingestion rejects every non-pass result and terminal enforcement exits non-zero. No workflow step reads `checks` or `status` before normalizer validation.
Requirements: REQ-M5-CI-008
ADRs: ADR-0042
Depends-On: DES-M5-CI-001 DES-M5-019
